## Research principles

**A candidate data source must earn incremental value.** The baseline is protected.

**Negative results remain visible.** They are part of the research path, not failed marketing.

**Persistence is not predictive value.** A coefficient can survive while its forecast contribution
dies.

**Model trust is dynamic.** Non-stationarity applies to models as well as individual signals.

**Complexity must be motivated by a failure mode.** Every major layer exists because the previous
simpler method exposed a specific weakness.

**Optimisation follows profiling.** C++ accelerates a measured bottleneck rather than serving as CV
decoration.

## Independence / confidentiality

This repository is independently developed using public data and synthetic tests. It contains no
employer data, code, models or proprietary research.
